homelab-invite (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: package the systemd unit -- debhelper reads debian/<pkg>.service,
    not the system/ source-of-truth copy, so the built 0.1.0 package
    silently shipped with no unit file at all (postinst's systemctl
    enable/start would have failed outright). Never deployed anywhere.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:05:00 -0500

homelab-invite (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: invite mechanism backend + public acceptance page.
    Own `invite` Postgres schema (invites/invite_quotas/verification_
    attempts), /internal/v1/invites/* fronted by homelab-api's
    /api/v1/invites/* gateway route, and the public /invite/:token
    acceptance page. Requires homelab-api >= 0.1.29 (invite_token
    support on /api/v1/auth/register + the gateway route) and
    homelab-common >= 0.1.23 (system_agent_token export).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500

